  "date": "2014-12",
  "title": "Peko Is Looking For New Members",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Further Information",
      "text": "Would you like to play an active role in promoting staff interests?\n\nThe ETH Zurich Personnel Committee (PeKo) is looking for motivated administrative or technical staff at ETH who are keen to get involved in personnel issues to join the committee for the 2015-2018 term.\n\nPeKo represents the interests of administrative and technical staff to the Executive Board of ETH Zurich and participates in dealing with current issues relating to personnel and university policy at ETH.\n\nIf you are interested in joining PeKo and willing to invest your time in it over the next four years, then we would be happy to receive your application.\n\nAll employees of ETH Zurich who have been working for ETH for at least six months on an ongoing and permanent basis and with an employment level of at least 50% FTE are eligible to apply. The term of office will begin in April 2015. The members elected to PeKo for the next four-year term will be informed personally.\n\nHave we sparked your interest? If so, please send us your application documents – including your personal details, a photo, a brief CV, details of your place of work and position and a covering letter – to the Head of the Election Office by 12 January 2015 at the following address:\n\nMr Cuno Künzler, Interim Head of Human Resources, Turnerstrasse 1, ETH-Zentrum, CH-8092 Zurich.\n\nPlease state the reference: “PeKo elections”."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Further Information",
      "text": "About the Personnel Committee: www.peko.ethz.ch\n\nAbout the elections: www.peko.ethz.ch/infos/reglement\n\nIf you have any questions, please contact:\n\nAndré Blanchard, President of PeKo Tel.: +41 44 633 26 03 E-Mail:\n\nJakob Hauri, Vice President of PeKo Tel.: +41 44 632 74 98 E-Mail:"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Further information",
      "text": "ETH Zurich Personnel Committee (in German)\n\nHR: Employment and Work News (ETH Intranet)"
    }
  ],
